# Taqathon site — working conventions

This project is worked on by both Claude Code and Cursor, split by task type
(Cursor for quick inline edits, Claude Code for multi-file features and the
git/PR/deploy workflow). These rules keep output consistent between the two.

## Read PROGRESS.md first

`PROGRESS.md` at the repo root is the authoritative, dated project log —
more reliable than any chat history. Read it before starting work you don't
have full context on.

**Standing rule: every PR that represents a meaningful checkpoint (a phase
completed, a real bug found and fixed, a significant decision made) must
append a short dated bullet to PROGRESS.md in that SAME PR** — not a
follow-up commit. Newest entries at the top. Bullets, not paragraphs: what
changed, why if not obvious, what's still open.

## Git workflow

feature branch → PR against `dev` → **wait for explicit user go-ahead**
("merge PR #N into dev") → **wait for explicit user go-ahead** to merge `dev`
into `main` (fast-forward). Never merge either step without being told to,
even if the PR looks obviously fine. GitHub Actions (`deploy.yml`) builds on
every push/PR to `main`/`dev` but only deploys on a direct push to `main`.

## Code comments

Every change needs thorough, plain-language comments explaining the WHY
(hidden constraints, workarounds, non-obvious history) — not just what the
code does. This is an explicit, standing preference for this project, not
the general terse-comment default.

## AR/EN parity

The site is bilingual (Arabic + English) via a pagination-over-a-locales-array
pattern — one template renders both language pages from paired
`*.ar.json`/`*.en.json` data files. **Never ship a change to one language
without the matching change to the other.** Content that can't yet be
published in both languages (e.g. a new Year Archive) should be held back
entirely rather than going live lopsided — see `src/_lib/years.js`, which
only surfaces a year once both language files exist.

## Hard-won context — do not redo this work

- **Netlify's OAuth-provider feature does not work for a placeholder/
  non-deployed site.** Decap CMS auth is handled by a self-hosted Cloudflare
  Worker instead (`cloudflare-worker/decap-oauth-worker.js`, deployed at the
  URL in `admin/config.yml`'s `base_url`). Cloudflare secret changes require
  clicking "Deploy" again on the Worker to take effect.
- Decap **folder collections need `extension`/`format` declared explicitly**
  (`extension: json, format: json`) — without it Decap defaults to Markdown
  and silently shows 0 entries, no error.
- Don't let a large asset folder (e.g. the gallery) be Decap's top-level
  default `media_folder` — it crashes the editor for every collection.
  Large folders get their own per-collection override.
- `editorial_workflow: true` is not supported with `local_backend`/local_fs —
  it silently downgrades to simple mode in local testing.

